error[E0960]: `fast.path x y` is not a type: it applies a relation to arguments
  --> tests/neg/e0960_applied_relation.hgn:22:28
   |
22 | instance : {x y : city} -> fast.path x y -> fast.path x y. (*~ E0960 *)
   |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an applied relation
   |
   = note: as a meta type, an applied relation would be `⇑(r t̄)`, the lift of a fact type of an application, which no object term has: the fact type of a relation `r` is `r` alone
   = note: an applied relation is a proposition of the program whose rules derive it
   = help: name the program in a judgment of `std/semantics`: `P ⊢ r t̄`

